# Interface Vision (Terminal/Hacker Theme)

Sidequest Mail should feel like a raw command line — but work like Proton Mail.
The monospace fonts are the skin, not the mechanics.
Everything below is aesthetic and optional; the core email flow (read, reply, file, delete) must always be instant.

---

## Layout Grid

| Screen       | Terminal Concept       | Behavior                                                                 |
|:-------------|:-----------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Inbox**    | The Command Line       | Emails are listed as text output. Unread emails have a blinking cursor.  |
|              |                        | Opening one "executes" it — the cursor moves to the next line.           |
| **Folders**  | The Directory          | Each folder is a directory path. Navigating there shows: `cd /sent`      |
| **Sent**     | Output Log             | You sent the command. "Exit Code 0" energy.                              |
| **Trash**    | /dev/null              | Where data gets deleted from the system. Dragging an email there erases it. |
|              |                        | Restoring it is `grep`-ing it back from the void.                        |
| **Drafts**   | The Buffer             | Still being typed. Cursor blinking, half-formed commands.                |

---

## Navigation Grid

| Key          | Action                 | Flavor Text                              |
|:-------------|:-----------------------|:-----------------------------------------|
| **Arrow Keys** | Move focus between emails | Terminal beep sound                  |
| **Spacebar**   | Open selected email    | `executing...`                           |
| **Enter**      | Reply while reading    | `send -y`                                |
| **Drag & Drop** | Move between folders   | `mv` command animation                   |

---

## Visual Design Grid

| Element        | Concept            | Description                                                                 |
|:---------------|:-------------------|:----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Sidebar**    | The Prompt         | Black background, green text. Looks like a bash prompt.                      |
| **Email Cards** | Text Blocks        | Each email is a block of monospace text. Unread blocks have a `>` prefix.    |
| **Compose**    | The Editor         | A raw text editor (like Vim/Nano). Subject line = `Subject:` header.         |
| **Stickers**   | ASCII Art          | Inserting a sticker adds an ASCII art character (e.g., `(^_^)`).             |

---

## Micro-interactions Grid

| Action         | Sound / Effect     | Trigger Context                          |
|:---------------|:-------------------|:-----------------------------------------|
| Reading        | Keyboard click     | Like typing a command                    |
| Replying       | Beep               | Like a successful command execution      |
| Deleting       | Static crackle     | Like file destruction                    |
| Searching      | Scanning tone      | Like a grep process                      |
| Composing      | Typing             | Like mechanical keyboard clacks          |
| Loading        | Progress bar       | Fills like a percentage counter          |

> All sounds default to **off**, toggleable in Settings → Audio.
> Silent mode is the default for a reason: this is still an email client people use at work.

